    "text_blocks": [
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "Yes, standard homeowners insurance policies in Utah typically cover hail damage under dwelling and property coverage. This pays to repair or replace damaged roofs, siding, gutters, and personal belongings, minus your specific policy deductible.",
        "reference_indexes": [
          0,
          1,
          2,
          3,
          4,
          5,
          6,
          7
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "What Is Covered"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Roofing: Cracks, dents, or broken shingles and damaged vents or flashing."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Exterior Structures:\nSiding, windows, exterior paint, and detached structures like a garage or shed."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Personal Property: Items inside your home if a roof or window breach leads to interior water damage."
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          11,
          12
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "heading",
        "snippet": "Important Policy Details"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Deductibles: Some insurers enforce a separate percentage-based or high-dollar deductible specifically for wind and hail claims rather than your standard all-peril deductible."
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Cosmetic Exclusions: Certain policies in storm-prone regions may exclude purely cosmetic damage (like minor dents that do not affect the function of metal roofs or siding).",
            "reference_indexes": [
              8
            ]
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Maintenance Issues: Damage resulting from a pre-existing lack of maintenance or old, worn-out roofing materials will not be covered."
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "You can review state consumer resources or file a dispute assistance request through the\nUtah Insurance Department\nif you encounter issues with a claim. Major providers like GEICO\nand Farmers Insurance\ninclude hail under standard Utah dwelling protections, but you should check your declarations page for specific deductible amounts.",
        "snippet_links": [
          {
            "text": "Utah Insurance Department",
            "link": "https://insurance.utah.gov/consumers/home-insurance/home-claims-info/"
          },
          {
            "text": "GEICO",
            "link": "https://www.geico.com/homeowners-insurance/states/ut/"
          },
          {
            "text": "Farmers Insurance",
            "link": "https://www.farmers.com/utah/home-insurance/"
          }
        ],
        "reference_indexes": [
          9,
          10
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "If you want to check your specific coverage, tell me:"
      },
      {
        "type": "list",
        "list": [
          {
            "snippet": "Your insurance provider"
          },
          {
            "snippet": "Whether you have a separate wind/hail deductible"
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "type": "paragraph",
        "snippet": "I can help you figure out what your out-of-pocket costs might be."
      }
    ],
